        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I'm working through the desiderative of the causative of aś (to eat): āśi + san gives āśayiṣa, and applying reduplication rules for vowel-initial roots, the second syllable reduplicates to form śiśayiṣ-.\n\nSo the correct form becomes āśiśayiṣati, paralleling how aṭ's causative desiderative gives āṭiṭayiṣati. Adding the prefix pra and the lṛṅ augment (vṛddhi ā), the conditional form works out to prāśiśayiṣiṣyatām.\n\nSince the causative is ubhayapada, and the desiderative follows the pada of its base, the parasmaipada ending here is correct.\n\n",
